s_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Coffee & Tea, Food","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"ompDR5sUDpoI6gnTldmneQ","review_id":"kHbCtEjpNQRsPD1bbmwerw","date":"2008-09-11T21:49:23","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9418382048606873,"text_excerpt":"i was there with a group of 14 other people and the praline connection was the last restaurant we visited before we returned home to Los Angeles. they were very accomodating with our group, pushing tables together so we could all sit together. since we had a large group that ordered a variety of items on the menu, i got to try a lot of delicious food that night! i ordered the fried chicken with mac and cheese and it came with cornbread. the fried chicken was deliciously crisp, but not greasy, moist, but not dripping with oil. it was awesome. cornbread was pretty good too. i also tasted a crabby gumbo that was....well....crabby. i won't go into details of the rest of the food that i tried,..."},{"business_id":"ompDR5sUDpoI6gnTldmneQ","review_id":"bZrjJ000kXOZVgenPIlqog","date":"2014-05-21T01:31:38","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9317358136177063,"text_excerpt":"My husband & I have been coming to New Orleans once a year for the past 15 years but have never ventured to the Marigny area. We're so glad we did tonight! It was a Tuesday night so many places along Frenchman were closed. We decided to try The Praline Connection and were seated immediately. Our waiter, Roland, greeted us warmly and brought our drinks quickly. I had the special: baked chicken (choice of white or dark meat) with cornbread dressing & gravy, greens, and a side salad. My chicken breast was crispy on the outside, moist and tender on the inside. The greens were tasty, especially with a splash of hot pepper liquid. The cornbread dressing was really good, too. My husband got the ..."},{"business_id":"ompDR5sUDpoI6gnTldmneQ","review_id":"0EXoQPa_NrkknWPBVgzNvw","date":"2018-09-13T12:40:44","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9278578162193298,"text_excerpt":"We enjoyed dinner here on our last night in NOLA. We split the Soul Food Sampler and just added an extra side of Mac and cheese and it was more food than my husband and i could finish together. Absolutely delicious! It took a while but the chicken was hot and obviously cooked to order so very much worth the wait! The drinks (hurricane and Jamaican me crazy) were also really good (and strong)!"}],"visual":[{"business_id":"ompDR5sUDpoI6gnTldmneQ","photo_id":"iC4XeEUwJzMUHx0r5zZthg","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/iC4XeEUwJzMUHx0r5zZthg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8775822520256042},{"business_id":"ompDR5sUDpoI6gnTldmneQ","photo_id":"Pv8xuvILo_uS3hSvm-e3PQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/Pv8xuvILo_uS3hSvm-e3PQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8541348576545715},{"business_id":"ompDR5sUDpoI6gnTldmneQ","photo_id":"hmxOY9aE1xisnNhzJ6eN2Q"